       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum in the labeling. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual 800 mg single-dose maximum. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this carries a real risk of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nCommon intended regimens would be:\n- **400 mg PO q6h PRN** (mild to moderate pain)\n- **600 mg PO q6h** (scheduled)\n- **800 mg PO TID or q8h** (up to 2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg QID is intentional, tell me and I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale, though I'd recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
